    {
      "label": "Errors fixed",
      "note": "out of 16 cases tested",
      "value": 3,
    },
    {
      "label": "New errors caused",
      "note": "none",
      "value": 0,
    },
  ],
  "lead": "Every repair is run case by case against the unchanged model on cases held back from the search, so a repair that only looks good on the cases it was designed against does not get through.",
  "points": [
    "Across 16 cases it was tested on, the best repair fixed 3 and broke 0.",
    "The evidence against that being luck runs only about 2.0 to 1, which is not strong enough to count.",
    "It applied to every failure it was aimed at — none was out of its reach.",
  ],
  "verdict": "1 repair was tested against the unchanged model, and none earned its place.",
}
`;
